<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="Anchor keeps the family’s shared moments in the group chat — a keeper of memories, not a person — so they can come back for everyone, especially Nikos."
  currentPath="/how-it-works"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How it works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Families already share their lives in group chats. Anchor sits in that circle as a keeper of those memories — never
      as a member of the family. No new app. The warmth comes from the people who shared the moments, not from the
      system.
    </p>

    <h2>The family invites Anchor</h2>
    <p>
      Together, the family adds Anchor to the group they already use. Nikos is part of that decision, not only the
      subject of it. He learns that Anchor is a keeper of photos and stories, not a person, and that one benefit is
      helping moments stay with him — without labelling him by a diagnosis.
    </p>

    <h2>Everyone shares</h2>
    <p>
      Sofia posts a photo of Maria’s first day of school with a few words. Later, Nikos shares an old photo of his own
      first day. Anchor keeps each moment with the words of the person who shared it. He is a contributor, not only a
      receiver.
    </p>

    <h2>Moments come back</h2>
    <p>
      Shared moments return over time — for Nikos a little more often, when he is usually rested. Each return is an
      invitation to relive the moment, not a question to answer correctly. Anchor attributes the memory to the person
      who shared it and never claims a shared past of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>The peak is contact</h2>
    <p>
      When he responds — often by voice — his detail becomes part of the memory. The family hears it and the
      conversation continues between people. Success is measured by that contact, not by how much anyone talks to
      Anchor.
    </p>

    <h2>Tender memories</h2>
    <p>
      Emotional memories, including painful ones, are not filtered out by default — they are often the ones that matter
      most. Nikos chooses, with the family’s support, which may come back, and that choice is revisited over time.
      Choices and stop live in the chat with Anchor. On the website, the family record hides moments marked sensitive;{' '}
      <a href="/my-data">My data</a> export includes them for their sharer.
    </p>

    <h2>On this website</h2>
    <p>
      Registration starts with your email, so you can read the privacy policy. Then you connect a family chat on the
      family page. Create the family name, then use the family page for the record. Uploads and Ask Anchor on the site are
      optional extras; everyday sharing belongs in the group chat.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/family">Get started</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/app">Try the scripted demo</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
